title: Genesis/Block
description: genesis widget distinguishes between block and inline
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki-multiple
tags: [[$:/tags/wiki-test-spec]]

title: Output

\whitespace trim
<$genesis $type="$reveal" type=nomatch>

Text block - $reveal creates a DIV. This text is covered in a P tag.
If you remove the leading line, reveal creates a SPAN, which covers this text.
New P tag now covers the reveal SPAN
</$genesis>

<$genesis $type="$reveal" type=nomatch $mode=block>

Block mode forced - $reveal creates a DIV. The leading line still decides this text, so it is covered in a P tag.
Remove the leading line and the P tag goes, but $reveal keeps its DIV because $mode says so
</$genesis>

<$genesis $type="$reveal" type=nomatch $mode=inline>

Inline mode forced - $reveal creates a SPAN. The leading line still decides this text, so it is covered in a P tag inside that SPAN.
$mode only picks the element for $reveal, it does not change how this body was parsed
</$genesis>

<$genesis $type=$reveal type=nomatch>Inline</$genesis>
<$genesis $type=$reveal type=nomatch $mode=block>Inline forced block</$genesis>
<$genesis $type=$reveal type=nomatch $mode=inline>Inline forced inline</$genesis>
